# Mechanical Mobster's two targets: "up to one target card from a graveyard" (either player's, and only from a graveyard) and "target creature you control". Bot1 casts a free
# Ornithopter on turn 1; on turn 2 Bot2 casts a free Ornithopter and a Black Lotus, sacrificing the Lotus (it is in Bot2's graveyard). On turn 3 Bot1 casts the Mobster with three
# Moxen. Bot2's Ornithopter (a battlefield permanent, not a graveyard card) and Bot2's Ornithopter as the creature (not Bot1's) are refused; the Lotus is exiled and Bot1's own
# Ornithopter connives: Bot1 draws and discards Forest, so no counter - the Ornithopter stays 0/2 and the Mobster 2/1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mechanical Mobster
Ornithopter
Forest
Mountain
Plains
Grizzly Bears
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mechanical Mobster.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Graveyard.Black Lotus)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Choose(Forest)

[Expect]
Exile.Count = 1
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Mechanical Mobster.Power = 2
Bot1.Graveyard = Forest
